ENFORCEMENT DECREE OF THE SSIREUM PROMOTION ACT

Article 1 (Purpose) The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters delegated by the Ssireum Promotion Act and matters necessary for the enforcement thereof.

Article 2 (Formulation of a Master Plan for the Promotion of Ssireum) (1) The term "matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 5 (2) 8 of the Ssireum Promotion Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") means the following matters:
1. Discovery, collection, and preservation of materials related to Ssireum;
2. Development and dissemination of content to promote Ssireum;
3. Inter-Korean exchanges and cooperation for the preservation and promotion of Ssireum.
(2) When the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism formulates a master plan for the promotion of Ssireum under Article 5 of the Act, the Minister shall notify the Special Metropolitan City Mayor, Metropolitan City Mayors, the Special Self-Governing City Mayor, Do Governors, the Special Self-Governing Province Governor, and the heads of Sis, Guns and Gus (referring to the heads of autonomous Gus) thereof.

Article 3 (Ssireum Day) (1) The State, local governments, Ssireum organizations, and other relevant bodies may hold the following events on Ssireum Day under Article 7 of the Act:
1. Ssireum competitions (including demonstration competitions);
2. Academic events related to Ssireum, such as seminars and forums;
3. Awards for persons who have rendered meritorious service to Ssireum;
4. Other events concerning the dissemination and promotion of Ssireum.
(2) The State and local governments may provide support if Ssireum organizations and other relevant bodies hold events under paragraph (1).

ADDENDUM <No. 23722, April 12, 2012>
This Decree shall enter into force on April 18, 2012: Provided, That the provisions concerning the Special Self-Governing City Mayor in Article 2 (2) shall enter into force on July 1, 2012.
